# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: cador-1-split-nihil-cador — name the two headless hosts nihil (stubs) and cador (CAD core)
#+STATUS: NEXT
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: infra
#+DEPENDS: cador-multidocument-host
#+BRANCH: cador

* Context

Sub-task 1 of the =cador-multidocument-host= epic (§1, §7). The epic
plans three hosts: =nihil= (no-op stubs), =cador= (headless in-process
CAD core), and a future wire host.

Code reality (verified 2026-08-06, master), which differs from the
epic's §7 assumption that entity code lives "in the null host":

- =autolisp-host/source/null-host.lisp= — the =null-host= class is
  ALREADY pure stubs: 51 methods, each =signal-host-not-supported= (a few
  sysvar-wiring ones are silent no-ops). This IS the intended =nihil=.
- =autolisp-mock-host/= — the =mock-host= class is the real headless CAD
  core (entity DB, ssget, symbol tables, dictionaries, sysvar catalogue,
  the vlax/vla COM surface, reactors). This IS the intended =cador=. It is
  the default backend (=--host mock=, and =resolve-host-backend= default).
- So the "split" the epic describes is, in this codebase, essentially a
  *rename to the epic's names* — the functional split (stubs vs CAD core)
  already happened, under the names null-host / mock-host.

(Note: the epic's "null host accumulated cador functions" framing pre-dates
the mock-host extraction; the accumulated functions are in mock-host.)

* Problem

The two headless hosts do not carry their intended architectural names,
and =nihil='s stub contract is a hard =:host-not-supported= error rather
than the softer "not implemented in this host" the owner wants for a
backend whose job is only to keep the interpreter running.

* Proposal

1. **cador = the real headless CAD host.** Rename =mock-host= →
   =cador= across package (=clautolisp.autolisp-mock-host= →
   =clautolisp.cador=), ASDF system, source directory, class,
   =make-mock-host= → =make-cador=, and the ~134 package refs / 140
   constructor sites / 45 files. Follow the epic §7 discipline: pure
   mechanical move/rename in one reviewable commit, no behaviour change.
2. **nihil = the stub host.** Rename =null-host= → =nihil= (7 files:
   class, =make-null-host=, =*null-host*=, package/system, docs).
3. **nihil stub behaviour.** Change the stubs from a bare
   =signal-host-not-supported= to the D1 taxonomy's *operation not
   supported by this host* condition, carrying a warning-grade message
   ("… not implemented in the nihil host") — visible, catchable, and
   distinct from cador's "unavailable in a headless context". (Exact
   condition-class vs warning semantics to align with D1 / owner; the
   pi/T/PAUSE-style predefined bindings and pure language surface must
   keep working under nihil.)
4. **CLI.** =--host cador|nihil= become the canonical values; keep
   =mock=→cador and =null=→nihil as accepted (deprecated) aliases so
   existing invocations, tests and docs do not break in one step.
5. **Tests.** Retain the mock-host suites under the cador name; the split
   the epic §7.7 wants (entity-semantics tests select cador, core-only
   tests select nihil) falls out naturally.

Open decision for the owner before executing (see the issue thread):
whether to do the full mock→cador rename now (large, churny, but the
epic's stated intent) or introduce =cador= as the canonical name with
=mock= kept as a thin alias to bound the churn.

* Acceptance criteria

- [ ] =cador= is the name of the real headless CAD host (class, package,
      system, constructor, =--host cador=), behaviour unchanged.
- [ ] =nihil= is the stub host (=--host nihil=); its operations signal the
      D1 "not supported by this host" condition with a clear message, and
      the pure language surface still runs under it.
- [ ] =mock= / =null= still accepted as deprecated =--host= aliases.
- [ ] Full =test-system "clautolisp"= green on SBCL and CCL.
- [ ] AGENTS.md / user-manual updated for the host names.

* Progress (2026-08-06, branch cador)

- **1a DONE (1.7.27).** mock-host → cador: dir, ASDF systems, package
  clautolisp.cador, class cador, make-cador, all *-accessors, 59 files.
  --host cador canonical, mock a deprecated alias. Suites green.
- **1b DONE (1.7.28).** null-host → nihil: class nihil, make-nihil,
  *nihil*, file nihil.lisp, tests nihil-tests.lisp. --host nihil
  canonical; null/none deprecated aliases. Suites green (host 30, cli 27),
  alfe still loads.

** OPEN — nihil stub semantics (warn-once-then-nil vs signal)

The chosen "warn-once-then-nil" was NOT applied, pending reconciliation:
nihil is the *default runtime host* (=*default-runtime-host*=), and its
=:host-not-supported= signalling is load-bearing —

- =(command "._LINE")= with no CAD host must ERROR (vendor semantics;
  evaluator test command-without-host-signals-host-not-supported);
- =vl-cmdf= "returns nil when host lacks command channel" works by
  *catching* that signal (test in builtins-core);
- ~23 tests assert :host-not-supported via the default/nihil host;
- the epic's own D1 condition taxonomy classifies this as a *condition*
  ("operation not supported by this host"), not a silent warn+nil.

Switching nihil to warn+nil would regress those AutoLISP semantics and
contradict D1. Recommended reconciliation: nihil keeps signalling the
catchable :host-not-supported condition (D1 taxonomy) with a clearer
"…not implemented in the nihil host" message — i.e. the "signal (clear
condition)" option — rather than warn+nil. Awaiting owner confirmation
before touching the stub bodies. (1a/1b renames keep current signalling.)
